{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1788281557,"nonce":"eCKYBe6HyP6QdtVPGwjgjnFneM0=","message":"RESOLVED BY INVESTIGATION — **`rwa` owns the IR dialect; the verb takes a\nresolved layout in ONE call.** Orchestrator, 2026-09-01, before dispatching\n`place-layout`.\n\n\nThis issue's scope says `place-layout {file.ir.json} --origin P`, which reads\nas \"the mod opens the file\". **The mod reads no IR today** — `File.ReadAllText`\nappears exactly twice in `Source/AutoRimmer/`, for `config.json` and the\njournal. So either the mod learns the KCSG/baseviz dialect, or something else\nexpands it first. That decision is most of the difference between a session and\nhalf a session, so it is settled here rather than discovered by a worker.\n\n\n**`rwa place-layout \u003cfile.ir.json\u003e --origin P` is the CLI surface** — what a\nperson types, and what this issue's scope describes. It parses the IR with\n`baseviz/ir.py`, the module that already IS the dialect, and sends the mod ONE\ncall carrying a resolved layout: a list of `{def, at, rot, stuff?}` plus the\norigin, mode and stuff-map.\n\n**The mod's verb never sees a file path or a token grid.**\n\n\n1. **Atomicity survives, which is the invariant that matters.** \"Preflight\n   EVERY cell first; on any failure place NOTHING\" cannot hold if `rwa` sends N\n   separate `build` calls — that is N transactions and a half-built room is\n   reachable. One call keeps the whole layout in front of the gate at once. This\n   is the reason the naive \"just loop `build`\" answer is wrong, and it is worth\n   stating because it is the tempting shortcut.\n2. **It is the project's own established split, not a new one.** 2.5's PNG\n   channel is exactly this shape — DESIGN, 2026-09-01: *\"no game-side image\n   rendering; a pure function of dump + catalog\"* — a whole channel deliberately\n   kept CLI-side so the mod stays Verse-only. `place-layout` is the same\n   argument with a different payload.\n3. **CLAUDE.md's ground rule says so directly:** \"the file half of the bridge\n   never touches Verse (analyzerbridge is the template).\"\n4. **One dialect, one parser.** `baseviz/ir.py` is vendored into this repo and\n   is the canonical reader. A second implementation in C# is a guaranteed drift\n   point, and `ir.py`'s own docstring already warns that XML→IR is lossy at the\n   edges (`_EXT_SCALAR`/`_EXT_LIST` whitelists, `size` derived from row lengths).\n   That is knowledge nobody should have to re-derive in another language.\n5. **A path the GAME must resolve is a machine-dependence bug waiting.** The\n   protocol is file-based through a root the bench owns; `rwa` runs where the\n   repo is. On BORGES those are different trees. A resolved payload has no path\n   in it and cannot mean two things.\n6. **The plumbing already exists on both ends.** `rwa --args-json` carries an\n   arbitrary nested object (`rwa/rwa:282`), and `DesignateEngine` already\n   accepts a `cells` list as a first-class target form\n   (`DesignateEngine.cs:120,135`). A 7x7 module is 49 cells; `freezer-kitchen`\n   is 66 across two layers. This is not a payload-size question.\n\n\nThe Scope's other bullets stand unaltered: preflight-every-cell,\n`--partial`, per-cell failures in `Blockers`' `{removal, reason}` shape,\nblueprint vs instant mode, `cancel-layout` by placement id, and explicit stuff\nresolution. `--origin P` is still a corner (`templates/INDEX.md` pin 1: the\ntoken sits in the footprint's north-west cell), and the corner→centre conversion\nis `Siting.cs`'s, already shipped — the layout verb must not write a second one.\n\n\nSession B built more of this than its brief asked for, so state it plainly for\nwhoever takes it: `SiteGate` is the preflight; `build` is the single-cell\nplacement; the **`Placements` registry** (`BuildVerbs.cs:410`) already maps\nid→placement, so `cancel-layout` is largely a query against it plus the shipped\n`designate {type:\"cancel\"}`; and **terrain is already handled** —\n`Siting.cs:446` resolves a `BuildableDef` as ThingDef then TerrainDef and\n`BuildVerbs.cs:347` branches on it, so floors are not new work. `site-audit`\nmakes \"instant ≡ built-blueprint\" provable, which #4 had called untestable.","files":null}]}